{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.DampingNonMonotoneWall","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DampingNonMonotoneWall","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.damping_route_walled","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.damping_route_walled","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DampingNonMonotoneWall.lean#L123-L138","doc":"**The damping route is walled — the required correction is non-monotone in A.**\nOn the canonical substrate window `[1.109, 1.11]`, the graded dimension undershoots\nA=3 (so a damping, which only subtracts, cannot close it — `damping_cannot_close_A3`)\nyet overshoots A=4 (`substrate_A4_overshoots`).  The residual therefore changes\nsign between A=3 (`+`) and A=4 (`−`); a multiplicative damping `D(A) ≤ 1` supplies a\nnon-positive correction at every A and cannot realise a sign change.\n\nThe statement packages the two directions as one certificate: at any substrate\n`q` in the window there is a damped-below A=3 value and an over-target A=4 value,\nso `damped A=3 < target(3)` while `target(4) < undamped A=4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.substrate_A4_overshoots","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.substrate_A4_overshoots","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DampingNonMonotoneWall.lean#L97-L121","doc":"**(O) A=4 overshoot.** For the canonical substrate window\n`1.109 ≤ q ≤ 1.11`, the (undamped) A=4 graded ratio strictly *exceeds* the A=4\nstrong target: `[3]_q·[4]_q > 13.0316` (`[3][4]_{1.109} = 15.702`).  At the same\nsubstrate where A=3 undershoots, A=4 overshoots — the correction the data wants is\n`+` at A=3 but `−` at A=4. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.damping_cannot_close_A3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.damping_cannot_close_A3","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DampingNonMonotoneWall.lean#L77-L95","doc":"**(U) A=3 undershoot / damping wall.** For the canonical substrate window\n`1 ≤ q ≤ 1.11` and ANY damping factor `0 ≤ d ≤ 1`, the damped A=3 ratio stays\nstrictly below the A=3 strong target: `d · [3]_q < 3.8128`.\n\n`[3]_q ≤ [3]_{1.11} = 3.3421 < 3.8128` (monotonicity + the substrate upper bound),\nand a damping only decreases it (`d · [3]_q ≤ [3]_q` since `d ≤ 1`, `[3]_q ≥ 0`).\nHence NO damping `D(A) ≤ 1` — parabolic/skew quotient (route a) or Demazure\nsub-crystal (route b) alike — reaches the A=3 anchor at the physical substrate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.dampGradRatio3_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.dampGradRatio3_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DampingNonMonotoneWall.lean#L73-L75","doc":"`[3]_q ≥ 0` on `q ≥ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.dampGradRatio3_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.dampGradRatio3_mono","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DampingNonMonotoneWall.lean#L67-L71","doc":"`[3]_q` is monotone increasing on `[1,∞)` (used for the substrate upper bound). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.dampGradStep4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.dampGradStep4","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DampingNonMonotoneWall.lean#L64-L65","doc":"`[4]_q = 1 + q + q² + q³`, the A=3→A=4 graded step (`ρ_grad(4) = [3]_q·[4]_q`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.dampGradRatio3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.dampGradRatio3","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DampingNonMonotoneWall.lean#L61-L62","doc":"`ρ_grad(3) = W_3/W_2 = [3]_q = 1 + q + q²`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}